Mechanism: If the OSPF↔EIGRP redistribution or boundary links were broken, 20.x↔120.x pings would fail; instead they pass, showing the ASBR is advertising/learning routes properly. Localization: r11 eth1 (111.x to r1) and eth0 (112.x to r12) are up and exchanging routes; r1’s and r12’s interfaces toward their respective LANs are healthy.

Root cause: No current fault; any prior outage during maintenance appears to have been resolved.

Corrective fix: No action required. Recommend monitoring. If intermittent issues recur, focus on r11’s redistribution policy and adjacencies on 111.x/112.x, as that’s the true routing boundary. === END ===